I'm not sure about whether changing this whole fine in this manner is useful, since most of it is the result of Protege 5.2.0 providing its OWL output in a different format than the version used to the create the ontology originally. I could instead:

Edit the file directly to remove the single-element property chain and to add the subproperty axiom, then test the ontology in Protege or our reasoner to make sure it can still be reasoned over. However, I suspect as a best-practice it's a good idea to always use Protege so we make sure we don't accidentally introduce issues.
See if I can change Protege's output so that it is more similar to the previous content (by using XML entities rather than XML namespaces).

