To run javascript once a page has loaded, you just need to surround the javascript code with:
$(function() {});

This tells the javascript inside to run once all the page is done loading.
If you are trying to change the height and the width of the element itself you could do something like this:
$(function() {
   $('.gal_link').height(345).width(605);
});

However, if you are trying to change the shadowbox properties in the rel of each link, you should do:
$(function() {
    $('.gal_link').attr('rel','shadowbox[gallery32];height=345;width=605');
});

